GRP = {'الوثائق والمخططات': 'Documents and Drawings', 'التشغيل والصيانة': 'Operation and Maintenance', 'الضمانات والشهادات': 'Warranties and Certificates', 'الترميز والتوسيم': 'Coding and Labelling', 'الاستلام والنظافة والسجلات': 'Acceptance, Cleaning and Records', 'فترة الضمان والاستلام النهائي': 'Warranty Period and Final Acceptance'}
STAGE = {'قبل الاستلام الابتدائي': 'Before provisional acceptance', 'عند الاستلام الابتدائي': 'At provisional acceptance', 'خلال فترة الضمان': 'During the warranty period', 'قبل الاستلام النهائي': 'Before final acceptance'}
HO = {
'HO-01': ('As‑Built Drawings', 'The Contractor shall submit as‑built drawings for all disciplines (architectural, structural, electrical, low current, mechanical, plumbing, fire fighting, medical gases, site works) reflecting the actual final condition, including routes of concealed services and locations of valves, panels and inspection points, approved and signed by the Contractor and the supervising engineer, using the room numbering approved by the Cluster.', 'Editable CAD (DWG) files + signed PDF + two bound A1 hard copies'),
'HO-02': ('Approved Shop Drawings and Submittal Register', 'The Contractor shall submit the final set of approved shop drawings, the submittal register with all submittals, their status and dates, and the register of requests for information (RFI) and change orders.', 'Indexed PDF + Excel register'),
'HO-03': ('Register of Installed Materials', 'The Contractor shall submit a register of all materials and equipment actually installed: product name, manufacturer, model, colour and finish number and batch number where applicable, supplier and contact details, and the material approval reference; to facilitate maintenance and like‑for‑like replacement in future.', 'Excel + technical data PDF'),
'HO-04': ('Photographic Record of Concealed Works', 'The Contractor shall document with dated photographs all works before they are concealed (inside ceilings and walls, under floors and insulation), classified by location and discipline, and submit them indexed with the as‑built drawings.', 'Photo folder indexed by building/floor/room'),
'HO-05': ('Operation and Maintenance (O&M) Manuals', 'The Contractor shall submit operation and maintenance manuals for every system and item of equipment in Arabic and English where possible, including: system description, start‑up and shut‑down procedures, periodic maintenance and its schedules, common faults and remedies, spare parts list, drawings and catalogues, and agent and technical support details.', 'Two bound, indexed hard copies + searchable PDF'),
'HO-06': ('Preventive Maintenance Schedule for Assets', 'The Contractor shall prepare a proposed preventive maintenance schedule for each asset per the manufacturer’s recommendations (task, frequency, duration, required skill, consumable spare parts) in the template approved by the Technical Services Department, so that it can be imported directly into the maintenance platform.', 'Excel in the approved template'),
'HO-07': ('Spare Parts and Attic Stock', 'The Contractor shall supply the spare parts recommended by the manufacturers for two years of operation of critical systems, and attic stock of finishing materials from the same batch of not less than: 2% of tiles and flooring, 2% of suspended ceiling tiles, and 5% of each paint colour in sealed, labelled containers, with a signed handover list.', 'Materials labelled and stored at the designated location + handover list'),
'HO-08': ('Special Tools', 'The Contractor shall hand over the special tools required to operate and maintain the equipment (panel keys, elevator tools, programming software and cables, administrator passwords of systems) with a handover list.', 'Signed handover list'),
'HO-09': ('Training of Operation and Maintenance Teams', 'The Contractor and equipment agents shall train the operation, maintenance, security and safety teams on operating and maintaining the systems and handling emergencies, through theoretical and practical on‑site sessions, with training material, video recording of the sessions and signed attendance sheets.', 'Approved training plan + attendance sheets + material and recordings'),
'HO-10': ('Facility Manual Data', 'The Contractor shall provide the Technical Services Department with the data required to issue the operation and maintenance manual and the facility user guide (R‑42): lists of systems and equipment and their locations, shut‑off and isolation points, contacts and warranties, and special instructions.', 'Per the facility manual template on the platform'),
'HO-26': ('Digital Signage per the Cluster Standard', 'The Contractor shall submit a display location schedule (location, model, size, height of the display centreline above finished floor level) complying with the Al Ahsa Health Cluster standard AAHC‑FM‑STD‑DIGITAL‑SIGNAGE‑001, with proof that every display in public areas is connected to the Navori platform, that two sockets and a wired network point are provided behind each display, and that all cables are concealed.', 'Excel schedule + a photo of each display after installation + IT confirmation of the Navori connection'),
'HO-11': ('General Works Warranty', 'The Contractor shall provide a general warranty for all works and materials for not less than one year from the date of provisional acceptance unless the contract or specifications require a longer period, during which the Contractor shall repair or replace any defect at its own cost.', 'Official stamped warranty letter'),
'HO-12': ('Manufacturers’ Warranties and Warranty Schedule', 'The Contractor shall submit manufacturers’ and agents’ warranties issued in the name of Al Ahsa Health Cluster, and a consolidated schedule showing for each system and item of equipment: warranty period, start and end dates, the warrantor and contact details. Minimum periods include: roof waterproofing 10 years, elevators two years, AC compressors 5 years, LED luminaires 5 years, automatic door operators two years.', 'Original warranties + Excel schedule'),
'HO-13': ('Test and Commissioning Certificates', 'The Contractor shall submit test and commissioning reports for all systems witnessed by the Cluster’s representative: electrical insulation and earthing tests, pressure tests of pipework and fire fighting, water quality and disinfection, air and water balancing (TAB), third‑party medical gas certification, elevator certification by an accredited inspection body, and device‑by‑device fire alarm testing.', 'Signed PDF reports + originals'),
'HO-14': ('Authority Certificates', 'The Contractor shall obtain at its own cost the certificates and approvals of the official authorities required for operation (Civil Defense, municipality, electricity company, water company and others depending on the project) and hand over the originals.', 'Original certificates'),
'HO-15': ('Material Conformity Certificates', 'The Contractor shall submit conformity certificates for materials and products subject to technical regulations (SASO) and fire rating certificates for doors, firestopping and rated glazing, matching what was actually installed.', 'Indexed PDF'),
'HO-16': ('Asset Coding and Register', 'The Contractor shall tag all electromechanical and medical equipment and assets with permanent, heat‑ and disinfectant‑resistant labels bearing a QR code per the coding system approved by the Cluster (Planon location code / building / floor / room / asset type / serial number), and submit the asset register (name, type, manufacturer, model, serial number, location, installation date, warranty expiry, supplier) in the platform template.', 'Installed labels + Excel register in the platform template'),
'HO-17': ('Room and Space Numbering', 'The Contractor shall apply the room and space numbering approved by the Cluster on doors, signs, as‑built drawings, electrical panels and fire alarm devices, so that the number matches across all documents and on site.', 'Room schedule + application on site'),
'HO-18': ('Labelling of Electromechanical Systems', 'The Contractor shall label: circuit schedules inside every electrical panel, cables at both ends, power and data outlets with the circuit/port number, pipes with identification colours and flow‑direction arrows, valves with numbered tags and a valve chart, ductwork, and medical gas outlets; and submit the fire alarm device address list.', 'Labelling on site + valve chart + circuit schedules'),
'HO-19': ('Keys and Access Cards', 'The Contractor shall hand over all keys labelled with the room number according to the approved master‑key system, with a key schedule, access cards programmed per the approved permissions, and the administrator passwords of the access control systems.', 'Key cabinet + schedule + handover record'),
'HO-20': ('Final Cleaning', 'The Contractor shall carry out comprehensive final cleaning of floors, walls, ceilings, windows, fittings, ductwork and filters, and terminal cleaning to infection control requirements of clinical areas before handover, removing all waste from the site.', 'Cleanliness inspection record'),
'HO-21': ('Removal of Temporary Works and Reinstatement', 'The Contractor shall remove all temporary structures, barriers and connections, and repair any damage to adjacent areas, routes or existing finishes, reinstating them to their original condition.', 'Inspection record'),
'HO-22': ('Snag List and Close‑out', 'The provisional acceptance record shall include a numbered, photographed snag list, which the Contractor shall close within the specified period, and the close‑out record shall be signed.', 'Snag list + close‑out record'),
'HO-23': ('Clearances and Claims', 'The Contractor shall submit clearances from subcontractors and main suppliers, settlement of temporary utility bills, and a declaration of no outstanding claims before payment of the final invoice.', 'Original declarations'),
'HO-24': ('Maintenance and Response During the Warranty Period', 'During the warranty period the Contractor shall respond to faults within 24 hours (within two hours for critical systems), carry out periodic preventive visits per the maintenance schedule, and record every visit and fault in a log submitted to the Technical Services Department.', 'Visit and fault log'),
'HO-25': ('Final Acceptance Requirements', 'Before final acceptance: joint inspection of all works, closing of warranty claims, updating the as‑built drawings with any modifications, renewal of expired certificates and submission of any remaining documents; then the final acceptance record is signed and the guarantees are released.', 'Final acceptance record'),
}
NOTES = [
('1. الأسعار مقطوعية شاملة جميع أعمال التوريد والتنفيذ والمواد والعمالة والمعدات والنقل والاختبار والتشغيل والتسليم والضمان والمصاريف العامة والأرباح.', '1. Prices are lump sum, inclusive of all supply and execution works, materials, labour, equipment, transport, testing, commissioning, handover, warranty, overheads and profit.'),
('2. المخططات والمواصفات وهذا الجدول وثائق مكملة لبعضها؛ وعند التعارض يُرجع للمهندس المشرف قبل التنفيذ ويُعتمد الأعلى مواصفةً. زيارة الموقع ومعاينة المناسيب والأبعاد إلزامية قبل التسعير.', '2. The drawings, specifications and this schedule are complementary documents; in case of conflict, the supervising engineer shall be consulted before execution and the higher specification shall apply. A site visit and inspection of levels and dimensions are mandatory before pricing.'),
('3. على المقاول دراسة المخططات وحساب جميع الكميات على مسؤوليته والاستفسار قبل التسعير؛ ولا تُقبل أي مطالبة بفروقات كميات أو أسعار أو أعمال ناتجة عن قصور الدراسة، ويُنفَّذ التصميم الخارجي والديكورات والبروزات كاملة كما في المخططات.', '3. The Contractor shall study the drawings, calculate all quantities at its own responsibility and raise queries before pricing; no claim for differences in quantities, prices or works resulting from insufficient study will be accepted, and the external design, décor and projections shall be executed in full as shown on the drawings.'),
('4. أي أعمال لازمة لإنجاز المبنى كاملاً جاهزاً للتشغيل تُعدّ مشمولة في المقطوعية ولو لم تُذكر صراحةً.', '4. Any works required to complete the building fully ready for operation are deemed included in the lump sum, even if not expressly stated.'),
('5. على المقاول إعداد الرسومات التنفيذية (Shop Drawings) لجميع الأعمال والتصاميم التكميلية حيث لا تكفي المخططات، بمهندسين مختصين وعلى حسابه، واعتمادها قبل التنفيذ، وتسليم مخططات كما نُفِّذ؛ وكل ذلك مشمول في السعر.', '5. The Contractor shall prepare shop drawings for all works and complementary designs where the drawings are insufficient, by specialist engineers at its own cost, have them approved before execution, and submit as‑built drawings; all of which is included in the price.'),
('6. الأكواد المرجعية: كود البناء السعودي بأبوابه (SBC 201/301/401/501/601/701/801) وNFPA وASHRAE وIEC، واشتراطات وزارة الصحة ومكافحة العدوى (IPC) ودليل الوصول الشامل.', '6. Reference codes: the Saudi Building Code and its parts (SBC 201/301/401/501/601/701/801), NFPA, ASHRAE and IEC, the requirements of the Ministry of Health and infection prevention and control (IPC), and the universal access guide.'),
('7. مناخ الأحساء وتربتها: أحمال التبريد على درجة تصميم خارجية لا تقل عن 46°م، وعزل جميع المواسير والدكت الخارجية ضد الشمس، ومواد مقاومة للأملاح والرطوبة، وأسمنت مقاوم للكبريتات وعزل أساسات مناسب للتربة السبخية حسب تقرير التربة.', '7. Al Ahsa climate and soil: cooling loads at an outdoor design temperature of not less than 46 °C, sun protection of all external pipes and ducts, salt‑ and moisture‑resistant materials, and sulphate‑resisting cement and foundation waterproofing suited to sabkha soil per the soil report.'),
('8. تُورَّد المواد جديدة أصلية من المصنّعين المعتمدين المذكورين في كل بند أو ما يعادلها بعد اعتماد خطي من الاستشاري، عدا ما وُصف بـ«حصراً». تُقدَّم العينات والبيانات الفنية ومخططات التصنيع قبل التوريد، وتُرفض أي مادة غير مطابقة وتُستبدل على نفقة المقاول دون تمديد للمدة.', '8. Materials shall be new and genuine from the approved manufacturers named in each item, or equivalent after written approval by the consultant, except those described as “exclusively”. Samples, technical data and fabrication drawings shall be submitted before supply; any non‑conforming material will be rejected and replaced at the Contractor’s cost without extension of time.'),
('9. المواد المستوردة طويلة التوريد (الديكورات وحماية الحوائط، المصعد، الأنظمة الخاصة) تُطلب مبكراً بما يتوافق مع الجدول الزمني، ولا يُعدّ تأخر الشحن مبرراً للتمديد.', '9. Imported long‑lead materials (décor and wall protection, the elevator, special systems) shall be ordered early in line with the time schedule; shipping delays shall not justify an extension.'),
('10. الظروف غير الظاهرة قبل الحفر (المياه الجوفية، التكهفات، تحسين التربة) تُعالج بأمر مستقل على حساب المالك وفق سعر السوق.', '10. Conditions not visible before excavation (groundwater, cavities, soil improvement) shall be addressed by a separate order at the Owner’s cost at the market rate.'),
]
